threads.body:
Straight loss here: `run_chat_streaming` used to accumulate the streaming finish reason, and now it's discarded without being moved anywhere — nothing else in this function sets `gen_ai.response.finish_reasons`, so the span ends up with no finish reason at all.

Compare `run_chat_streaming_reference` in `reference/scenarios/openai/scenario.py` and `run_chat_streaming` in `reference/scenarios/mistralai/scenario.py`: both keep the accumulator and promote it to the response attribute. The mock's final chunk carries `finish_reason: "stop"` (`reference/src/semconv_genai/mock_server/openai.py`), and the deleted code already read `chunk.choices[0].finish_reason`, so this is capturable from the stream rather than hardcoded:

```suggestion
        text = ""
        finish_reasons = []
        for chunk in resp:
            if chunk.choices[0].delta.content:
                text += chunk.choices[0].delta.content
            if chunk.choices[0].finish_reason is not None:
                finish_reasons.append(chunk.choices[0].finish_reason)
        if finish_reasons:
            span.set_attribute("gen_ai.response.finish_reasons", finish_reasons)
```

